sudo apt install git -y


TOPIC 1: GIT CONFIGURATION
===========================

Check Git version              | git --version
Check Git config               | git config --list
Set username                   | git config --global user.name "Your Name"
Set email                      | git config --global user.email "you@example.com"
Check username                 | git config user.name
Check email                    | git config user.email
Set default branch             | git config --global init.defaultBranch main


TOPIC 2: GIT REPOSITORY
=======================

Create directory               | mkdir project
Go inside directory            | cd project
Initialize Git repository      | git init
Check repository status        | git status
Show hidden files              | ls -la
Remove Git repository          | rm -rf .git


TOPIC 3: GIT BASIC WORKFLOW
===========================

Initialize repository          | git init
Check status                   | git status
Stage file                     | git add file.txt
Stage all files                | git add .
Commit changes                 | git commit -m "Initial commit"
Add remote                     | git remote add origin <URL>
Push code                      | git push -u origin main


TOPIC 4: GIT FILE OPERATIONS
============================

Create file                    | touch file.txt
Add file                       | git add file.txt
Add all files                  | git add .
Remove file                    | git rm file.txt
Rename file                    | git mv old.txt new.txt
Check status                   | git status


TOPIC 5: GIT STAGING
====================

Stage file                     | git add file.txt
Stage all files                | git add .
Unstage file                   | git restore --staged file.txt
Unstage all files              | git restore --staged .
View unstaged changes           | git diff
View staged changes             | git diff --cached


TOPIC 6: GIT COMMIT
===================

Create commit                  | git commit -m "message"
Commit all tracked changes     | git commit -am "message"
View commits                   | git log
One-line history               | git log --oneline
Last 5 commits                 | git log -5
Show commit                    | git show <commit-id>
Show commit graph              | git log --oneline --graph --all


TOPIC 7: GIT BRANCH
===================

List branches                  | git branch
List remote branches           | git branch -r
List all branches              | git branch -a
Create branch                  | git branch feature
Switch branch                  | git switch feature
Create and switch branch       | git switch -c feature
Delete branch                  | git branch -d feature
Force delete branch            | git branch -D feature
Rename branch                  | git branch -m new-name


TOPIC 8: GIT CHECKOUT
=====================

Switch branch                  | git checkout main
Create branch                  | git checkout -b feature
Restore file                   | git restore file.txt
Restore file from commit       | git restore --source <commit> file.txt


TOPIC 9: GIT REMOTE
===================

Add remote                    | git remote add origin <URL>
View remote                   | git remote -v
Remote details                | git remote show origin
Change remote URL             | git remote set-url origin <URL>
Rename remote                 | git remote rename origin upstream
Remove remote                 | git remote remove origin


TOPIC 10: GIT PUSH
==================

Push current branch           | git push
Push main                     | git push origin main
First push                    | git push -u origin main
Push feature branch           | git push -u origin feature
Push all branches             | git push --all
Delete remote branch          | git push origin --delete feature
Force push                    | git push --force
Safe force push               | git push --force-with-lease


TOPIC 11: GIT FETCH
===================

Fetch remote changes           | git fetch
Fetch origin                   | git fetch origin
Fetch all remotes              | git fetch --all
Remove deleted branches        | git fetch --prune


TOPIC 12: GIT PULL
==================

Pull latest changes             | git pull
Pull from main                 | git pull origin main
Pull using rebase              | git pull --rebase


TOPIC 13: GIT MERGE
===================

Merge branch                   | git merge feature
Abort merge                    | git merge --abort
Continue merge                 | git merge --continue


TOPIC 14: MERGE CONFLICT
========================

Check conflict                 | git status
After resolving conflict       | git add .
Complete merge                 | git commit
Abort merge                    | git merge --abort


TOPIC 15: GIT REBASE
====================

Rebase branch                  | git rebase main
Interactive rebase             | git rebase -i HEAD~3
Continue rebase                | git rebase --continue
Abort rebase                   | git rebase --abort
Skip commit                    | git rebase --skip


TOPIC 16: GIT STASH
===================

Save changes                   | git stash
Save with message              | git stash push -m "WIP"
List stashes                   | git stash list
Apply stash                    | git stash apply
Apply and remove stash         | git stash pop
Delete stash                   | git stash drop stash@{0}
Delete all stashes             | git stash clear


TOPIC 17: GIT RESET
===================

Unstage file                   | git reset file.txt
Reset previous commit          | git reset HEAD~1
Soft reset                     | git reset --soft HEAD~1
Mixed reset                    | git reset --mixed HEAD~1
Hard reset                     | git reset --hard HEAD~1


TOPIC 18: GIT REVERT
====================

Revert commit                  | git revert <commit-id>
Revert latest commit           | git revert HEAD
Continue revert                | git revert --continue
Abort revert                   | git revert --abort


TOPIC 19: GIT TAG
=================

List tags                      | git tag
Create tag                     | git tag v1.0.0
Create annotated tag           | git tag -a v1.0.0 -m "Release"
Show tag                       | git show v1.0.0
Push tag                       | git push origin v1.0.0
Push all tags                  | git push origin --tags
Delete local tag               | git tag -d v1.0.0
Delete remote tag              | git push origin --delete v1.0.0


